hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23587","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Amr ibn Muadh al-Ashhali, from his grandmother, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O believing women, let none of you despise her neighbor, even a burnt sheep hoof."
"23623","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Damrah ibn Sa'id from his grandmother from a woman among them, and she had prayed the two qiblas with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to me: Dye with henna; one of you leaves dye until her hand is like the hand of a man. She said: So she never left dye until she met Allah Almighty, and she used to dye though she was eighty."
"23624","Haytham ya'ni Ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us from Ibn Harmalah from Abu Thifal al-Muzani that he said: I heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib say: My grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no prayer for one without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar."
"23625","Sa'id ibn Khuthaym Abu Ma'mar al-Hilali narrated to us, my grandmother Rub'iyyah daughter of Iyad al-Kilabiyyah narrated to me, she said: I heard Ali say: Eat pomegranate with its pulp, for it tans the stomach."
"23626","Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Sabbah from Ashras, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about the ebb and flow, and he said: An angel is entrusted with the depths of the sea; when he puts his foot it overflows, and when he lifts it it recedes."
"23627","And he said: Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to me, Salih ibn Sabbah narrated to us from his father from Ashras from Ibn Abbas the like of it."
"23628","Sufyan ya'ni Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah: That Maryam lost Isa, peace be upon him, so she went about seeking him; she met a weaver and he did not guide her, so she supplicated against him, and he remains bewildered; then she met a tailor and he guided her, so she supplicated for him, and so they are sociable, i.e. sat with."
